Local changes include GTK onboarding/settings/tray, gesture handling, waveform
presentation, microphone capture, per-session transport cancellation, credential
storage and offline packaging. This product uses Doubao cloud recognition only;
it does not bundle a local speech recognition engine.

Distributions must retain LICENSE and NOTICE. Bundled dependency wheels retain
their embedded license files; see packaging/DEPENDENCIES.md in the source tree.

macOS source provenance:
The initial Swift implementation under macos/Sources/ was imported from
lilong7676/doubao-murmur commit 7549daf8f669eed38f1f2b4ac7cfadae8d17b0c6.
AudioCaptureManager.swift, AppState.swift, OverlayPanel.swift, OverlayView.swift,
and the DoubaoASRParams data type retain adapted upstream code. The application
entry point, credential store, hotkey handling, transport lifecycle, login window,
transcription controller and protected paste implementation were reworked here.
macos/Resources/inject-*.js are copies of the inherited Linux login resources.
The upstream MIT license is retained at macos/UPSTREAM-LICENSE and in Mac bundles,
alongside this repository's LICENSE and NOTICE. No upstream updater is included.
The optional Mac polishing policies, default prompts, gesture semantics, official
ASR framing and AU05 protocol are ports of this repository's Linux implementation.

The native macOS voice envelope, speech cadence, basketball pose keyframes and waveform rendering are adapted from this repository’s Linux ui/voice_motion.py, ui/basketball_motion.py and ui/waveform.py.
